/*
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/settings.json
!/rules/
# skills/ is deny-by-default, whitelisted one skill at a time. The directory holds more than this
# repository's own skills: org skills sync into skills/synced/ on a managed machine, and anything
# installed from a third party lands beside them. None of that is part of this config, and a
# blanket !/skills/ made every one of them an untracked file one `git add skills/` away from the
# public remote. A new skill of this repository's own must add its own line below;
# scripts/health-check.sh's skill-tracking check fails on any skills/*/SKILL.md that git does not
# track, so a missing line is loud rather than a skill silently absent from the commit meant to
# add it. A foreign skill nested a level deeper, as an org sync writes it
# (skills/synced/<skill>/SKILL.md), is skipped by that check on structure alone; only one
# installed flat beside this repository's own needs naming in skills-foreign.local.
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/cursor-projection/
!/skills/deep-review/
!/skills/execute-plan/
!/skills/go-dev/
!/skills/health-check/
!/skills/research/
!/skills/review-md/
!/skills/skill-author/
!/skills/write-plan/
!/agents/
!/commands/
!/hooks/
!/scripts/

!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/reference/
!/specs/
!/decisions/
!/evals/

# .health-check-stamp (repository root) records this machine's last full scripts/health-check.sh
# run - its date, the commit it ran against, and how many findings it produced - which
# scripts/session-setup-check.sh reads to nudge when a run is overdue or left findings
# unaddressed. It needs no rule here for the same reason as scrub-patterns.local below, and must
# never gain a !/ line: "when did this machine last audit the tree" is per-machine state, and a
# tracked stamp would tell every clone it had been audited because one of them had.

# scrub-patterns.local (repository root) holds this machine's client and engagement patterns for
# scripts/scrub-check.sh. It needs no rule here: the leading /* ignores every root entry that is
# not explicitly whitelisted above, so it cannot be committed by accident. Never add a
# !/scrub-patterns.local line - a tracked list of client names would be the exact leak that check
# exists to prevent.

# skills/<name>-workspace/ is where the skill-creator plugin writes eval run output: executor
# transcripts and native grading JSON. Those can carry real machine state - an eval that runs a
# --check against this machine pulls ~/.cursor MCP server names and absolute home paths straight
# into the transcript. The /skills/* rule above already ignores them; this stays as a named,
# explained rule so the reason survives any future loosening of that line. Never add a ! line
# for it, and never whitelist a workspace the way a skill directory is whitelisted.
skills/*-workspace/
